  "final_message": "I refactored `inBodyStartTag` in `src/main/java/org/jsoup/parser/HtmlTreeBuilderState.java`. `mvn -B clean test` passes: 2648 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS. This is the only file I changed; I didn't touch anything under `src/test`.\n\n**What changed**\n- **The method is now just a dispatcher.** It went from about 355 lines to about 100. Each `case` now calls a small private method (`inBodyStartA`, `inBodyStartLi`, `inBodyStartBody`, `inBodyStartFrameset`, `inBodyStartSelect`, `inBodyStartDdDt`, etc.), and the old `default` branch moved to `inBodyStartOther`.\n- **Duplicated code was pulled into shared helpers:**\n  - `closePInButtonScope`: the \"if there's a `p` in button scope, close it\" check, which was repeated about 9 times.\n  - `inBodyStartGeneric`: reconstructs formatting elements and inserts the element (used for `span`, the final fallback, and `option`/`optgroup`).\n  - `inBodyStartFormatter`: reconstructs, inserts and pushes the element onto the active formatting list (the formatting tags and `a`).\n  - `inBodyStartForeign`: `math` and `svg`, parameterised by namespace.\n- **Related tags were grouped together:**\n  - `textarea`, `xmp`, `iframe` and `noembed` go to `inBodyStartRawText`.\n  - `option` and `optgroup` go to `inBodyStartOptionGroup`.\n  - `rb`, `rtc`, `rp` and `rt` go to `inBodyStartRuby`.\n- **The local variables shared across the whole switch are gone** (`stack` and `el`). Each helper now declares its own.\n- **Some `else` branches were replaced with early returns** (in `body`, `frameset` and `image`), which makes the flow easier to follow.\n\n**How I kept the behaviour the same**\nEach helper makes the same calls in the same order as the original and returns the same `boolean` values. One case needed extra care: for `nobr` I didn't reuse `inBodyStartFormatter`, because that would add a `reconstructFormattingElements()` call the original code doesn't make."
 },
